createdby: DBot
description: 'Sets the access control list (ACL) permissions for an existing Amazon
  S3 bucket in a specified AWS account and region. Allows you to define who can access
  the bucket and what actions they can perform using predefined (canned) ACLs. Use
  this action to remediate cloud posture issues by setting the bucket ACL to ''private''
  to remove public access grants. Since 2023, all new S3 buckets block ACLs by default
  for better security. This is a remediation action that modifies bucket configuration.
  REQUIRES: `account_id`, `region`, and the resource identifier. When these are not
  present in user input, resolve them first via `CortexListAssets` using the issue''s
  asset_id or asset_name.'
